Box families follow tcolorbox by Thomas F. Sturm. The wobble is written in
pure Typst after the Rough.js and TikZ sketch techniques. jotter-polylux (Andreas Kröpelin, MIT) inspired the sloppy
frame and the post-it fasteners.
The *antique* vintage effect (`src/antique.typ`) draws its engraved strokes
with the nibart package (MIT) and is MIT like the rest of the package.

This MIT license applies to the original faboxyst source except for files
that carry a separate license notice:

- `src/pgfornament.typ` is derived from pgfornament and distributed under
  LPPL 1.3c.
- `src/tornpage.typ` is derived from a work distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
- The demonstration SVGs in `examples/assets/` are distributed under MIT-0.

Those files retain their respective license terms; they are not relicensed
under MIT by this notice.

No fonts are bundled. Use whatever faces are installed on the system.
